# Untrusted BSC JSON-RPC (headers + eth_getProof). Do not commit real keys.
# docker compose reads this file; the image does not contain the URL.
# Prefer a provider that can eth_getProof by block number. Since 2026-08-25 reads resolve
# to the BLS-finalized head (~2 blocks behind tip), so the window a provider has to serve
# is small and most free keyless endpoints clear it -- see docs/proof-provider-matrix.md.
# Only `run --finality confirmation-depth` still needs the old ~110-block window.
HELIOS_BSC_UPSTREAM=https://YOUR_BSC_HTTPS_RPC

# Optional transport failover if the primary errors (still untrusted; not a soak oracle).
# HELIOS_BSC_BACKUP=https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org

# Local verified RPC (helios-bsc run) and an independent soak oracle.
#
# Three different hosts, and the reason is not tidiness. The oracle exists to disagree
# with the upstream, so it cannot be the upstream. The checkpoint oracle confirms the
# root of trust, so it cannot be whichever host wrote that checkpoint, and it cannot be
# the upstream that will then serve the proofs -- either way it would be confirming a
# thing against itself. This file used to name the same host for both oracles.
#
# The oracle must also serve the `parlia_` namespace for `--finality fast`; most public
# BSC endpoints answer -32601. publicnode does.
# HELIOS_BSC_LOCAL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
# HELIOS_BSC_ORACLE=https://bsc-rpc.publicnode.com
# HELIOS_BSC_CHECKPOINT_ORACLE=https://bsc-dataseed.bnbchain.org
